// Custom detection rule deleted
//
// Fires when someone deletes a custom detection rule. Deleting detections is a cheap way
// to blind a SOC.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  Medium
// MITRE:     T1562.001
// Tables:    CloudAppEvents
// Custom details: RuleName
//
// Needs:
//   - The Defender for Cloud Apps Microsoft 365 connector with Microsoft 365 activities
//     turned on.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check who deleted it, which rule, and the ticket.
//   - Escalate if there's no ticket, or it's one of the rules in this folder.
//   - Close if it's a ticketed cleanup.
//
// Based on: Bert-Jan Pals' post, https://kqlquery.com/posts/audit-defender-xdr/

CloudAppEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where ActionType == "DeleteCustomDetection"
| extend RuleName = tostring(RawEventData.RuleName)
| project Timestamp, ReportId, AccountObjectId, AccountDisplayName, IPAddress, RuleName
